# WSClean CLI arguments for the smoke test, one per line (blank lines and
# '#' comments ignored). Read by scripts/smoke-test-wsclean.sh. The MS
# path and -name output prefix are appended by the script itself.
#
# 256x256 / 1000 clean iterations / mgain 0.8 keeps this a genuine, if
# tiny, gridding -> iFFT -> deconvolution pass on the ~530 KB JVLA
# minimal test MS, completing in well under a minute on one thread.
-size
256
256
-scale
1asec
-niter
1000
-mgain
0.8
-auto-threshold
3
-j
1
# The MS fixture is bind-mounted read-only (kept pristine across re-runs);
# this skips WSClean's normal write-back of predicted model visibilities
# into the MS, which would otherwise fail with a "Read-only file system"
# error at the very end of an otherwise-successful run.
-no-update-model-required
